---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Image to STL Converter"
  description="Terms of service for the free Image to STL Converter. Usage terms, liability, and intellectual property information for our browser-based 3D conversion tools."
  canonical="https://www.image-2-stl.com/terms/"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 mb-10">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">
        By using image-2-stl.com, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Service Description</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">
        image-2-stl.com provides free, browser-based tools for converting images to 3D model files (STL, OBJ, GLB). All processing occurs locally in your browser. No files are uploaded to our servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Your Content</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-2">You retain all rights to:</p>
      <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-surface-500 list-disc pl-5 mb-4">
        <li>The images you upload for conversion</li>
        <li>The STL, OBJ, and GLB files generated by the tool</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">
        You may use the generated 3D model files for personal projects, commercial products, sale on marketplaces, or any other purpose. We claim no ownership or rights over your output.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">You agree not to use the service to create content that is illegal, harmful, or infringes on the intellectual property rights of others.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Disclaimer</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed mb-2">The service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We make no guarantees about:</p>
      <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-surface-500 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>The accuracy or printability of generated 3D models</li>
        <li>Uninterrupted or error-free service availability</li>
        <li>Compatibility with specific 3D printers or slicer software</li>
        <li>The suitability of generated models for any particular purpose</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, image-2-stl.com and its operators shall not be liable for any damages arising from the use or inability to use the service. Always verify your 3D models in a slicer before printing and follow your printer manufacturer safety guidelines.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">
        Questions about these terms? Contact us at <strong class="text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300">hello@image-2-stl.com</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
